CAP={'Fig1':'Fig. 1. Present-day soil carbon. (a,b) Probability density of SOC and SIC stocks per 10′ cell by depth (dashed lines = medians); inset: share of each layer in the 0–200 cm total. (c,d) SOC and SIC stocks 0–30 cm with continent shares (inset). (e,f) 0–200 cm stocks with area proportion per class (inset). Grey = not applied (no prediction).',
 'Fig2':'Fig. 2. Inorganic carbon share of total soil carbon. (a) SIC/(SOC+SIC) 0–200 cm. (b) Top 18 countries by total carbon (colour = continent). (c) Country SOC versus SIC share; dashed lines = medians, bold numbers = % of countries per quadrant. (d) Circular bar chart of SIC share for the 36 largest SIC-holding countries grouped by continent.',
 'Fig3':'Fig. 3. Climate-driven change. (a) Density of equilibrium ΔSOC 0–30 cm by SSP (inset: % area losing/gaining). (b) Density of ΔSOC and ΔSIC 0–200 cm, SSP5-8.5. (c–f) Classed maps of change (Mg C ha⁻¹), 2081–2100, six-GCM mean, equilibrium (space-for-time). Totals and time-limited estimates in Fig. S13.',
 'Fig4':'Fig. 4. Nitrogen acidification. (a) Density of cropland ΔpH by scenario (Huang ΔpH = −0.06·Nin + 0.11, ISIMIP IMAGE N). (b) Countries with largest SIC loss, SSP5-8.5. (c,d) SIC loss maps with continent shares (inset). (e) Global topsoil SIC loss.',
 'Fig5':'Fig. 5. Bivariate SOC–SIC response (0–200 cm, SSP5-8.5, equilibrium). (a) Map with 2×2 legend and % land area per quadrant. (b) Country ΔSOC vs ΔSIC (symlog) with % of countries per quadrant. (c) Continental totals.',
 'Fig6':'Fig. 6. Mineral-associated (MAOC) and particulate (POC) organic carbon. (a) Density of MAOC and POC stocks. (b) Future ΔMAOC and ΔPOC 0–30 cm (equilibrium, bars = GCM range; and time-limited by 2100 with τ_POC = 15 yr, τ_MAOC = 150 yr). (c) f_MAOC 0–30 cm. (d) MAOC stock 0–30 cm. (e) Bivariate MAOC vs POC (split at global medians). (f) Global MAOC 0–100 cm vs Georgiou et al. 2022 (gridded product summed on all cells; dashed = published 899 Pg non-permafrost).',
 'Fig7':'Fig. 7. Drivers of soil-carbon components. (a) Grouped mean |SHAP| (%) for pH, SIC presence, SIC amount, mineral SOC and f_MAOC. (b–d) Dominant driver group per cell. (e–h) Partial dependence with piecewise-linear breakpoints (dashed).'}
