H(doc,'Drivers of SOC, MAOC, POC, SIC and pH (v8)',2)
P_(doc,"Methods. Exact TreeSHAP contributions (XGBoost pred_contribs) on 30,000 random land cells; features grouped into Climate (19 bioclim, PET, aridity), Soil (texture, CEC, predicted pH), Topography (elevation, slope, TPI) and Parent material (GLiM classes). Vegetation and N-deposition covariates are not in the fitted stack, so these groups cannot be attributed (limitation). Dominant-driver maps use approximate SHAP on all cells. Partial dependence with two-segment breakpoints; a standardized linear path model on WoSIS points tests direct and indirect (via pH) aridity effects.")
P_(doc,'Grouped importance (% of mean |SHAP|): '+'; '.join(f"{k}: "+', '.join(f"{g} {v:.0f}" for g,v in S[k]['group_pct'].items() if v>0.5) for k in S)+'.')
P_(doc,'Top features: '+'; '.join(f"{k}: "+', '.join(f"{n} ({v:.0f}%)" for n,v in S[k]['top_features'][:3]) for k in S)+'.')
P_(doc,f"Thresholds (PDP breakpoints): SIC presence vs log aridity {PD['SIC_presence_vs_logAI']['breakpoint']:.2f} (logAI = ln(1+P/PET); P/PET ≈ {np.expm1(PD['SIC_presence_vs_logAI']['breakpoint']):.2f}), vs MAP {PD['SIC_presence_vs_MAP']['breakpoint']:.0f} mm, vs pH {PD['SIC_presence_vs_pH']['breakpoint']:.2f}; f_MAOC vs clay {PD['fMAOC_vs_clay']['breakpoint']:.0f}%, silt {PD['fMAOC_vs_silt']['breakpoint']:.0f}%, CEC {PD['fMAOC_vs_CEC']['breakpoint']:.0f}; mineral SOC vs MAT {PD['SOC_vs_MAT']['breakpoint']:.1f} °C. Observed WoSIS pH–SIC logistic: pH₅₀ = {OB['logistic_pH50']:.2f} (n = {OB['n']:,}), i.e. the sigmoid shape reported by Huang et al. (2024, Fig. 3).")
P_(doc,f"Path analysis (n = {sem['n']:,}): aridity → pH β = {sem['pH']['logAI']:.2f}, pH → SIC β = {sem['SIC']['pH']:.2f}, direct aridity → SIC β = {sem['SIC']['logAI']:.2f}, indirect via pH {sem['indirect_AI_pH_SIC']:.2f} (R² pH {sem['pH']['R2']:.2f}, SIC {sem['SIC']['R2']:.2f}, SOC {sem['SOC']['R2']:.2f}). Linear paths are descriptive and do not replace the non-linear SHAP results.")
for k in ['Fig7']:
  for f in sorted(glob.glob(FM+f'/{k}_*.png')): doc.add_picture(f,width=Inches(6.5)); caption(doc,CAP[k])
CN8=(f"1）新增 MAOC/POC：采用 Georgiou 2022 开放合成数据（含 ISRAD、LUCAS 子集），剔除 POC=0/未测记录后 n={cv['n']}，随机10折 R²={cv['R2_fMAOC']:.2f}（首次含未测POC的0.63被判定虚高并重做）。0–30 cm MAOC {a['MAOC']:.0f} Pg（{a['MAOC_CI90'][0]:.0f}–{a['MAOC_CI90'][1]:.0f}）、POC {a['POC']:.0f} Pg；0–100 cm MAOC {a['MAOC']+b['MAOC']:.0f} Pg，对比 Georgiou 已发表 899 Pg（非冻土）与其栅格全域求和 {G['grid_sum_0_30']+G['grid_sum_30_100']:.0f} Pg。"
 f"2）未来：SSP5-8.5 平衡态 ΔMAOC {sc['585']['dMAOC_eq']:.0f}、ΔPOC {sc['585']['dPOC_eq']:.0f} Pg；到2100时限响应 ΔPOC {sc['585']['tl_central']['dPOC']:.0f}、ΔMAOC {sc['585']['tl_central']['dMAOC']:.0f} Pg。"
 "3）驱动因素：SHAP 分组重要性、依赖图、PDP 阈值、主导驱动图、路径分析，并与 Huang Fig.3 pH–SIC 曲线对照；植被/N 沉降未进入协变量，属局限。4）全部主图（7）与支撑图（13）按 Nature Food 风格重绘：Robinson 投影、离散色阶+“Not applied”、左下角插图柱状图、双变量 2×2 图例、密度曲线+中位线、国家棒棒糖图、象限散点、玫瑰图。")
